{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAotSa3PMkhWEu3DxTMr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XN26wjVoXzma9sUD5ZBZ4W","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-W4WnsT && python3 - <<'E'\np='bin/nightly-review.zsh'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''cd \"$REPO\" || { \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review: repo missing\"; exit 1; }\n\nclaude -p \"$PROMPT\" --output-format text > \"$OUT\"\nstatus=$?\n\nif [ $status -ne 0 ]; then\n  \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED (exit $status), see $OUT\"\n  exit $status\nfi\n\n\"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review done: $(head -c 300 \"$OUT\")\"\n''','''# NB: never assign to `status` in zsh (read-only builtin); use rc.\n# Report failures loudly: also log to stderr if the notifier itself fails.\nfail() {\n  print -u2 -r -- \"$(date '+%F %T') $1\"\n  \"$NOTIFY\" \"$1\" || print -u2 \"notify.sh failed\"\n}\n\ncd \"$REPO\" || { fail \"nightly review: repo missing\"; exit 1; }\n\nSTART=$SECONDS\n# Prompt goes via stdin, not a multi-line argument.\nprint -r -- \"$PROMPT\" | claude -p --output-format text > \"$OUT\"\nrc=$?\nDUR=$((SECONDS - START))\nprint -r -- \"$(date '+%F %T') claude rc=$rc duration=${DUR}s bytes=$(wc -c < \"$OUT\")\"\n\nif [ $rc -ne 0 ]; then\n  fail \"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc, ${DUR}s), see $OUT\"\n  exit $rc\nfi\n\n# Exit 0 is not proof of work: require real output.\nif [ ! -s \"$OUT\" ]; then\n  fail \"nightly review produced EMPTY output (${DUR}s)\"\n  exit 2\nfi\n\n\"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review done (${DUR}s): $(head -c 300 \"$OUT\")\"\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>\n''','''    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>\n    <key>USER</key>\n    <string>vk</string>\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\nzsh -n bin/nightly-review.zsh && plutil -lint Library/LaunchAgents/*.plist\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Why nightly-review was silent\n\n`launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6`, `last exit code = 1`: the job fired every night\nand failed. The logs (`Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`) show two stacked causes:\n\n1. **`Not logged in · Please run /login`** – under launchd the plist's environment had\n   only `PATH`; no `USER`, so the `claude` CLI could not find its login in the keychain\n   and died immediately. Fix: add `USER=vk` to `EnvironmentVariables` in the plist.\n   (Also: pass the prompt via stdin, `print -r -- \"$PROMPT\" | claude -p ...`, rather than a\n   multi-line argument.)\n2. **`nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status`** – the script did `status=$?`.\n   In zsh `status` is a read-only builtin, so assigning to it aborts the script before it\n   reaches the failure notification. The failure reporter was downstream of the failure,\n   so Telegram never heard anything. Fix: use `rc=$?`.\n\n## Changes\n- `bin/nightly-review.zsh`: `rc` instead of `status`; prompt piped via stdin; failures go\n  through a `fail()` helper that also logs to stderr; logs duration/bytes; treats empty\n  output (exit 0 but no work) as a failure; success message includes duration.\n- `Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`: added `USER`.\n\n## To apply and verify (on the real machine; I could not run launchd here)\n```\nlaunchctl bootout gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review\nlaunchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist\nlaunchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review\nlaunchctl print gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review   # last exit code = 0\n```\nConfirm the output file is fresh and non-empty, the run took a plausible time (not a few\nseconds), and the Telegram \"done\" message arrived. Then force a failure once (e.g. rename\nthe repo path) and confirm the failure message arrives.\n\nAlso check: `notify.sh` reads the token from the keychain, so it too relies on `USER`\nbeing set (now fixed). The README says 02:30 while the plist uses 02:30 as well; unchanged.\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2370,"cache_read_input_tokens":21841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2370},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5fbcbe9-e2b4-4944-86dd-0801c14d8e18","uuid":"c905f25f-eb74-4b34-96d2-31577d8f1edc","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:30:17.986Z","request_id":"req_011CgAotSJAh7vHbHCW7pzKF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XN26wjVoXzma9sUD5ZBZ4W":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-W4WnsT && python3 - <<'E'\np='bin/nightly-review.zsh'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''cd \"$REPO\" || { \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review: repo missing\"; exit 1; }\n\nclaude -p \"$PROMPT\" --output-format text > \"$OUT\"\nstatus=$?\n\nif [ $status -ne 0 ]; then\n  \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED (exit $status), see $OUT\"\n  exit $status\nfi\n\n\"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review done: $(head -c 300 \"$OUT\")\"\n''','''# NB: never assign to `status` in zsh (read-only builtin); use rc.\n# Report failures loudly: also log to stderr if the notifier itself fails.\nfail() {\n  print -u2 -r -- \"$(date '+%F %T') $1\"\n  \"$NOTIFY\" \"$1\" || print -u2 \"notify.sh failed\"\n}\n\ncd \"$REPO\" || { fail \"nightly review: repo missing\"; exit 1; }\n\nSTART=$SECONDS\n# Prompt goes via stdin, not a multi-line argument.\nprint -r -- \"$PROMPT\" | claude -p --output-format text > \"$OUT\"\nrc=$?\nDUR=$((SECONDS - START))\nprint -r -- \"$(date '+%F %T') claude rc=$rc duration=${DUR}s bytes=$(wc -c < \"$OUT\")\"\n\nif [ $rc -ne 0 ]; then\n  fail \"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc, ${DUR}s), see $OUT\"\n  exit $rc\nfi\n\n# Exit 0 is not proof of work: require real output.\nif [ ! -s \"$OUT\" ]; then\n  fail \"nightly review produced EMPTY output (${DUR}s)\"\n  exit 2\nfi\n\n\"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review done (${DUR}s): $(head -c 300 \"$OUT\")\"\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>\n''','''    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>\n    <key>USER</key>\n    <string>vk</string>\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\nzsh -n bin/nightly-review.zsh && plutil -lint Library/LaunchAgents/*.plist\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Why nightly-review was silent\n\n`launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6`, `last exit code = 1`: the job fired every night\nand failed. The logs (`Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`) show two stacked causes:\n\n1. **`Not logged in · Please run /login`** – under launchd the plist's environment had\n   only `PATH`; no `USER`, so the `claude` CLI could not find its login in the keychain\n   and died immediately. Fix: add `USER=vk` to `EnvironmentVariables` in the plist.\n   (Also: pass the prompt via stdin, `print -r -- \"$PROMPT\" | claude -p ...`, rather than a\n   multi-line argument.)\n2. **`nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status`** – the script did `status=$?`.\n   In zsh `status` is a read-only builtin, so assigning to it aborts the script before it\n   reaches the failure notification. The failure reporter was downstream of the failure,\n   so Telegram never heard anything. Fix: use `rc=$?`.\n\n## Changes\n- `bin/nightly-review.zsh`: `rc` instead of `status`; prompt piped via stdin; failures go\n  through a `fail()` helper that also logs to stderr; logs duration/bytes; treats empty\n  output (exit 0 but no work) as a failure; success message includes duration.\n- `Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`: added `USER`.\n\n## To apply and verify (on the real machine; I could not run launchd here)\n```\nlaunchctl bootout gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review\nlaunchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist\nlaunchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review\nlaunchctl print gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review   # last exit code = 0\n```\nConfirm the output file is fresh and non-empty, the run took a plausible time (not a few\nseconds), and the Telegram \"done\" message arrived. Then force a failure once (e.g. rename\nthe repo path) and confirm the failure message arrives.\n\nAlso check: `notify.sh` reads the token from the keychain, so it too relies on `USER`\nbeing set (now fixed). The README says 02:30 while the plist uses 02:30 as well; unchanged.\nE"}}}
