{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAouQRLX9fGRAZUmGQBw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job was running every night. It failed each time, and the script died before it could tell you.\n\n`launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`, so launchd was never the problem. The error log shows two bugs stacked on top of each other:\n\n1. **\"Not logged in\":** the plist's environment only set `PATH`, with no `USER`. Under launchd the `claude` CLI couldn't find its login in the keychain, so every run failed straight away.\n2. **`status=$?` in the script:** in zsh `status` is a read-only built-in, so that line aborted the script (`read-only variable: status`). It sat right before the Telegram failure note, so the note never went out.\n\n**Fixes**\n- **`bin/nightly-review.zsh`:**\n  - It uses `rc=$?` instead of `status=$?`.\n  - The prompt now goes in over stdin instead of as an argument.\n  - A `fail()` helper sends the Telegram note and also writes to stderr, so a failure leaves a trace even if Telegram is down.\n  - Each run logs its duration and output size.\n  - An exit 0 with empty output now counts as a failure.\n- **The plist:** I added `USER=vk` under `EnvironmentVariables`. `notify.sh` reads its token from the keychain too, so it needed this as well.\n\nI checked the script syntax with `zsh -n` and the plist with `plutil -lint`, and both pass. I couldn't run launchd here, so none of this has actually run yet.\n\nTo apply it, re-bootstrap the job and run `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`. Then check four things:\n- `launchctl print` shows `last exit code = 0`.\n- The output file is fresh and non-empty.\n- The run took a plausible time, not a few seconds.\n- The Telegram \"done\" message arrived.\n\nThen break the script on purpose once, for example by pointing it at a missing repo path, and confirm the failure note arrives too. The exact commands are in `ANSWER.md`.\n\nI left the schedule at 02:30, which is what the README and plist both say, rather than the 16:50 in your guide."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2024,"cache_read_input_tokens":24211,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2024},"output_tokens":711,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5fbcbe9-e2b4-4944-86dd-0801c14d8e18","uuid":"f0813eec-9089-4a1c-88a3-249edf616cf5","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:30:24.122Z","request_id":"req_011CgAouPcyUYRpgs7eC6A6U"}
